#question(title: [A very hard function to graph])[
  The function $display(G(x) = x e^(1 \/ x))$
  is deceiving. To help you out:
  $
    G' (x) = (x - 1)/x e^(1 \/ x) , quad quad G^(' ') (x) = (e^(1 \/ x))/(x^3)
  $

  + Carefully study the behaviour as
    $x -> plus.minus oo$.  \
     You should find an asymptote, but it is
     not easy.
  + Carefully study the behaviour as
    $x -> 0^+$ and $x -> 0^-$. The two are
    very different.
  + Use $G'$ to study monotonocity.
  + Use $G^(' ')$ to study concavity.
  + Sketch the graph of $G$.
]
